== Abstract ==

This BIP defines the derivation scheme for HD wallets which create timelocked addresses used for creating fidelity bonds. It also gives advice to wallet developers on how to use fidelity bonds to sign over messages, such as certificates, which are needed when using fidelity bonds that are stored offline.

Three versions of the scheme are defined: Version 1, the original scheme already deployed in JoinMarket; Version 2, a revision using a dedicated derivation <tt>purpose</tt> and a Miniscript-compatible <tt>witness script</tt>; and Version 3, a Taproot ([[bip-0341.mediawiki|BIP341]]) variant of Version 2's script, committed as the sole leaf of a script-path-only Taproot output. Wallets SHOULD create new fidelity bonds using Version 2 or Version 3, and SHOULD also recognize Version 1 and Version 2 fidelity bonds that already exist.

